.TH SSHM 1 "2026-10-17" "sshm 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.
.SH NAME
sshm \- manage, organize and connect to the hosts in ~/.ssh/config
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sshm
.br
.B sshm
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ ARGS ]
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sshm
edits
.I ~/.ssh/config
for you and connects to its hosts. The SSH config stays the only source of
truth: plain
.B ssh
keeps working exactly as before.
.PP
Edits are lossless. Only the lines of the fields you change are rewritten;
comments, formatting, repeated directives,
.B Match
blocks, wildcard hosts and
.B Include
directives are kept byte for byte. Hosts in
.BR Include d
files are listed and edited where they live. Multi-alias lines such as
.B "Host db db\-alias"
are supported.
.PP
Run without a command on a terminal to open the interactive picker.
.
.SH PICKER
The picker uses the whole screen. Type to fuzzy-filter by name, alias, user,
hostname and tags.
.B @tag
keeps hosts with a tag starting with
.IR tag ;
.B /folder
keeps hosts in a folder starting with
.IR folder .
Hosts you connected to recently come first.
.TP
.BR Up / Down ", " Ctrl\-P / Ctrl\-N ", mouse wheel"
Move the selection.
.TP
.BR PgUp / PgDn
Move a page.
.TP
.B Tab
Mark or unmark the selected host. With two or more marked,
.B Enter
opens them as tabs (see
.BR TABS ).
.TP
.B Enter
Connect to the selected host.
.TP
.B Mouse click
Select a row; click the selected row again to connect.
.TP
.BR Ctrl\-U ", " Ctrl\-W
Clear the query, delete the last word.
.TP
.BR Esc ", " Ctrl\-C
Quit.
.
.SH TAGS AND FOLDERS
.B Tags
are labels; a host can have many. They are stored in a comment line that
.B ssh
ignores:
.PP
.RS
.nf
Host web
    # sshm: tags=prod,web
    HostName 10.0.0.1
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B Folders
are real files. Folder
.I work/acme
is
.IR ~/.ssh/sshm.d/work/acme.conf .
A host lives in exactly one place: the main config or one folder file.
The first time a folder is created, sshm adds one
.B Include
line at the top of
.I ~/.ssh/config
so that ssh loads every folder file. Folders nest up to three levels.
.
.SH TABS
.B sshm open
(or marking hosts in the picker) opens one tab per host. Tabs run on sshm's own
tmux server
.RB ( "tmux \-L sshm" ,
tmux 3.0 or newer), so the user's tmux configuration and sessions are not
affected. Inside an existing tmux session, hosts open as new windows of that
session instead.
.TP
.BR "click a tab" ", " Alt\-Left / Right ", " Shift\-Left / Right ", " Alt\-1 .. 9
Switch tabs.
.TP
.BR "click [ + ]" ", " Alt\-N
New tab with the picker; the chosen host replaces it.
.TP
.B Alt\-W
Close the tab (after confirmation).
.TP
.B Alt\-R
Reconnect. A tab whose connection fails or drops stays open and shows
.BR "connection closed" .
.TP
.B Alt\-D
Detach. The tabs keep running;
.B sshm tabs
returns to them.
.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Hosts
.TP
.B sshm list \fR[\fB\-\-search\fR \fITEXT\fR] [\fB\-\-tag\fR \fITAG\fR]... [\fB\-\-folder\fR \fIFOLDER\fR] [\fB\-\-tree\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR table|json|compact] [\fB\-\-detailed\fR] [\fB\-\-all\fR]
List hosts. Optional columns (key, jump, forward, folder, tags) appear only
when some host uses them.
.B \-\-folder /
means the main config.
.B \-\-tree
groups hosts by folder. Long lists are paginated to the terminal height
.RB ( \-\-page ", " \-\-per\-page ", " \-\-all ).
.TP
.B sshm show \fINAME\fR [\fB\-\-raw\fR]
Show one host.
.B \-\-raw
prints its block exactly as written in the file.
.TP
.B sshm search \fIQUERY\fR [\fB\-\-limit\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-min\-score\fR \fIN\fR]
Rank hosts by fuzzy score against
.IR QUERY .
.TP
.B sshm add \fR[\fB\-\-name\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-hostname\fR \fIH\fR] [\fB\-\-user\fR \fIU\fR] [\fB\-\-port\fR \fIP\fR] [\fB\-\-identity\-file\fR \fIF\fR] [\fB\-\-proxy\-jump\fR \fIJ\fR] [\fB\-\-local\-forward\fR \fISPEC\fR] [\fB\-\-tag\fR \fIT\fR]... [\fB\-\-folder\fR \fIF\fR]
Add a host. Prompts for the rest when name, hostname or user is missing.
.I SPEC
is
.B 8080:localhost:80
or
.BR "8080 localhost:80" .
.TP
.B sshm update \fINAME\fR [\fB\-\-new\-name\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-hostname\fR \fIH\fR] [\fB\-\-user\fR \fIU\fR] [\fB\-\-port\fR \fIP\fR] [\fB\-\-identity\-file\fR \fIF\fR] [\fB\-\-proxy\-jump\fR \fIJ\fR] [\fB\-\-local\-forward\fR \fISPEC\fR]
Change fields of a host; prompts for every field when no option is given.
Pass
.B \-
to clear an optional field, e.g.
.BR "\-\-proxy\-jump \-" .
.TP
.B sshm rename \fINAME NEW_NAME\fR
Rename a host or one of its aliases.
.B ProxyJump
references in other hosts are updated.
.TP
.B sshm copy \fISOURCE NEW_NAME\fR
Clone a host, with all options and comments, into the same file.
.TP
.B sshm remove \fINAME\fR [\fB\-\-force\fR]
Remove a host after confirmation; warns when other hosts jump through it.
.SS Connecting
.TP
.B sshm
Open the picker and connect to the chosen host.
.TP
.B sshm open \fR[\fINAME\fR | \fB@\fItag\fR | \fB/\fIfolder\fR]... [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-extra\-args\fR \fIARGS\fR]
Open hosts as tabs.
.BI @ tag
and
.BI / folder
expand to every matching host. Without arguments the picker opens.
.TP
.B sshm tabs \fR[\fB\-\-close\fR]
Attach to the open tabs, or close them all.
.TP
.B sshm connect \fR[\fINAME\fR | \fB@\fItag\fR | \fB/\fIfolder\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-extra\-args\fR \fIARGS\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-fuzzy\fR]
Connect to a host. An unknown name falls back to fuzzy matching: one strong
match (\(>=\~90%) is used directly, otherwise the picker opens with the name
as query. Without a name, or with
.BI @ tag
or
.BI / folder ,
the picker opens. sshm runs
.BI "ssh \-\- " NAME
(plus
.B \-F
when
.B config_file
is not
.IR ~/.ssh/config ),
so ssh resolves the whole config itself.
.B \-\-dry\-run
prints the command instead.
.TP
.B sshm test \fINAME\fR [\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fISECONDS\fR]
Check TCP reachability (skipped behind
.B ProxyJump
or
.BR ProxyCommand ),
then a non-interactive login with
.BR BatchMode=yes .
Prints
.B [ OK ]
or
.B [FAIL]
and exits non-zero on failure.
.SS Organizing
.TP
.B sshm tag add \fINAME TAG\fR...
.TQ
.B sshm tag rm \fINAME TAG\fR...
.TQ
.B sshm tag list
Add or remove tags, or list every tag with its host count.
.TP
.B sshm folder add \fIFOLDER\fR
.TQ
.B sshm folder rm \fIFOLDER\fR
.TQ
.B sshm folder list
Create a folder, delete an empty one, or show the folder tree.
.TP
.B sshm mv \fINAME FOLDER\fR
Move a host into
.I FOLDER
(created if needed);
.B /
moves it back to the main config. The block moves unchanged.
.SS Data and settings
.TP
.B sshm export \fR[\fB\-\-output\-file\fR \fIFILE\fR]
Write every host (with tags and folder) to JSON.
.TP
.B sshm import \fIFILE\fR [\fB\-\-overwrite\fR]
Import a file written by
.BR "sshm export" .
.TP
.B sshm backup \fR[\fB\-\-output\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR]
Back up the config and every folder file. Manual backups are never rotated.
.TP
.B sshm config show \fR|\fB get \fR[\fIKEY\fR] |\fB set \fIKEY VALUE\fR
Show or change settings:
.RS
.TS
l l l.
Key	Default	Description
_
config_file	~/.ssh/config	SSH config to manage
folders_dir	~/.ssh/sshm.d	Folder files
backup_dir	~/.ssh/backups	Automatic backups
auto_backup	true	Back up before writing
max_backups	20	Kept per file (0 = all)
default_key	(none)	Suggested by sshm add
.TE
.RE
.TP
.B sshm man \fR[\fB\-\-install\fR | \fB\-\-uninstall\fR]
Show this manual.
.B \-\-install
copies it to
.I ~/.local/share/man/man1
so that
.B man sshm
works.
.TP
.B sshm \-\-version
Print the banner and version.
.TP
.B sshm \-\-install\-completion
Install shell completion for host, tag and folder names.
.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SSHM_CONFIG
Path of the settings file instead of
.IR ~/.ssh\-manager/config.json .
Handy to try sshm on a copy of your config.
.TP
.B SSHM_NO_ANIM
Disable the logo sweep and typing effects. They are already off when
output is not a terminal.
.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.ssh/config
The OpenSSH config file.
.TP
.I ~/.ssh/sshm.d/
Folder files
.RI ( name .conf,
nested in subdirectories).
.TP
.I ~/.ssh/backups/
Backups:
.IB file . timestamp .bak
(automatic, rotated) and
.IB file . timestamp .manual.bak
(from
.BR "sshm backup" ).
.TP
.I ~/.ssh\-manager/config.json
sshm settings.
.TP
.I ~/.ssh\-manager/history.json
Last connection time per host (picker order).
.TP
.I ~/.ssh\-manager/tmux.conf
tmux configuration for the tabs, regenerated every time tabs are opened.
.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success,
.B 1
on errors, otherwise the exit status of
.BR ssh .
.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR ssh_config (5)
.
